  "transcript_asr": "the source mentions a maximum conversation lifetime of 24 hours. Yes. The built -in ontology agent's conversation history only lasts within your current browser session. Wait, really? If you refresh the page, close the browser tab or hit the 24 hour mark, that entire conversational history is permanently gone. So under no circumstances should a team use the chat window as their permanent knowledge repository or decision log? Absolutely not. The chat is strictly an ephemeral scratch pad. The durable, permanent knowledge must be saved in the ontology definitions themselves,",
